**Exact comparison (real binary input shapes as captured by harness logic vs native shims):**
Harness emits/collects arbitrary JSON inputs actually sent by models to the grok binary's registered tools (via ACP tool call params "input" or flat). Native shims define the Input + JsonSchema that native xAI grok models see.
- todo_write: harness collects inputs with "todos": Vec< {content, status, [active_form/id?]} > (per note at 584 + PLAN jq refs to plan-and-todo-samples)
  native: TodoWriteInput { todos: Vec<GrokPlanItem {content, status: PlanEntryStatus (snake), active_form?}> }
- enter_plan_mode: harness: params for "enter_plan_mode" containing plan vec (or todos)
  native: EnterPlanModeInput { plan: Vec<GrokPlanItem>, explanation? }
- monitor: harness: "command", "cd", "description?", "timeout_ms?"
  native: MonitorInput { command, cd: String (req), description?, timeout_ms? } -- delegates Terminal + authorize + Terminal content
- spawn_agent: harness: persona + (capability_mode per G-20)
  native: SpawnAgentToolInput { label, message, persona?, capability_mode?, session_id? } -- good match
- Plan items: harness samples show Grok shapes (content/status); native update_plan uses step/status (PlanItem). Different for fidelity.

